1
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Two Films. One Love.

2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
The Disappearance of Eleanor Rigby: Her is a drama,
romance film directed by Ned Benson.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Told from the woman's perspective, the story of a couple trying to reclaim the life and love
they once knew and pick up the pieces of a past that may be too far gone.

4
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Eleanor Rigby, played by Jessica Chastain.

5
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Conor, played by James McAvoy.

6
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Professor Lillian Friedman, played by Viola Davis.

7
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Mary Rigby, played by Isabelle Huppert.

8
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Julian Rigby, played by William Hurt.

9
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Katy Rigby, played by Jess Weixler.

10
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
The Disappearance of Eleanor Rigby is the collective title of three films written and directed by Ned Benson in his directorial debut, and starring Jessica
Chastain and James McAvoy, alongside a supporting cast of Viola Davis, Bill Hader, Katherine Waterston, Ciarán Hinds, Isabelle Huppert, and William Hurt.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
After the film split into three parts, Him and Her  were screened at the 2013
Toronto International Film Festival as a "work in progress".

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Them premiered in the Un Certain Regard section
of the 2014 Cannes Film Festival.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
Them premiered in the United States on September 12, 2014, while Him and Her
were released together as double feature on October 10, 2014.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The film explores themes of new york city, loss of loved one, couple.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
The tone is emotional.
